    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0265" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg231"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr.
                            Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 395.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that your dispatch No.
                    324, of the 21st ultimo, reporting that Mr. Casimir Hartmann, a naturalized
                    American citizen of German birth, had been discharged from enforced service in
                    the German army, has been received.</p>
                <p>Your communication has been read with satisfaction, especially in view of the
                    fact that this case establishes our contention as to the applicability of the
                    principles of our naturalization treaties to the territory of the
                    Reichland-Alsace-Lorraine.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
